    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0561" n="1147" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p2/pg1147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Policy Planning Staff Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Policy Planning
                        Staff</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d328-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-07-08">July 8, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Attached is a paper designed to suggest the sort of program we feel might be put
                    in hand to create a new and hopeful atmosphere in our East and South Asian
                    policy.</p>
                <p>Since the schedule embodied in this paper is only intended to be illustrative,
                    and does not represent any final Staff recommendation, I am not making it a
                    Staff paper. But I hope it will serve to show what we have in mind as <hi
                        rendition="#italic">the sort of</hi> program we consider possible and
                    necessary, without committing us to certain of the individual proposals (such as
                    that for a three-power defense treaty) which obviously require careful study and
                    airing before they could be seriously considered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi> F. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Kennan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d328-a1.xml" xpointer="d328-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d328-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d328-f1-content">
                <p>Submitted to the Under Secretary of State (Webb), Ambassador at Large Philip C.
                    Jessup, Counselor Charles E. Bohlen, and the Deputy Under Secretary of State
                    (Rusk).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
